{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nobrega8/mbmap-library/main/schema/mbmap-2.schema.json",
  "mbmap": 2,
  "vendor": "Chauvin Arnoux",
  "model": "ENERIUM 100/200/300 V2",
  "models": [
    "ENERIUM 100",
    "ENERIUM 200",
    "ENERIUM 300",
    "ENERIUM 310"
  ],
  "vendor_website": "chauvin-arnoux.com",
  "description": "Panel-mounted power and energy analysers with RS-485 Modbus RTU and Modbus TCP",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-10-18",
  "source": "Chauvin Arnoux Energy, Definition de l'interface Modbus des centrales de mesure ENERIUM 100/200/300 V2, MS0-7423 Ed05",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "MS0-7423 Ed05, Interface Modbus ENERIUM 100/200/300 V2 (French)",
      "url": "https://www.chauvin-arnoux-energy.com/sites/default/files/HLHBSJS4.PDF",
      "note": "Annex 3, Modbus addressing; annex 1, standard types"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "All 32-bit values take two registers with the most significant word first (the manual shows the serial number as MSB at 0x0003 and LSB at 0x0004); each register is big-endian. The units below follow the manual's resolution column: voltages 1/100 V, currents 1/10000 A, powers in W, var and VA, frequencies 1/100 Hz.",
    "Reads use function 3 or 4 (the same data) and are limited to 125 registers. Settings are not written to the 0x68xx configuration area, which is read only: they are changed with command words. Write the command code to 0xD000 and its arguments from 0xD001 with function 16 (for example 0x0200 sets the slave address, 0x0201 the RS-485 speed, 0x0202 the parity, 0x0203 the stop bits).",
    "Not mapped: minima and maxima with their dates (0x0AE4 to 0x0CFE and 0x0B34 to 0x0CBE), the 51-point harmonic spectra (0x0600 to 0x07F8), the averaged harmonics (0x1102 and up), the alarm FIFO (0x0F00), alarm, HMI, digital and analogue I/O configuration (0x6842 to 0x6CBC), recording and load curves (0x6DAE and up), power quality (ENERIUM 300 only) and the MAC address (0x001E to 0x0023).",
    "Power factor and cos phi are followed by a quadrant register (0 inductive, 1 capacitive). Average powers are split into consumed (receiver) and generated values; the manual's generated side has no sign convention beyond the name.",
    "Serial settings: 9600 bit/s, no parity and 1 stop bit are the defaults (formats F10 to F12); the optical front port is fixed at 38400 bit/s, 8 data bits, no parity, 1 stop bit and accepts any slave address. Modbus TCP listens on port 502. ASCII mode is selectable but this map is for RTU/TCP.",
    "The command words that are not valid on a given product version answer with exception 3.",
    "The alarm status word is 32 bits wide (0x0200 and 0x0201): the high register holds the global alarm state in bits 0 to 7 and the global alarm memory in bits 8 to 15; the low register holds the 16 elementary alarms."
  ],
  "protocol": "tcp+rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baudrate": 9600,
  "data_bits": 8,
  "parity": "N",
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "max_read_registers": 125,
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
